    {
      "block": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "source": "sections/sec-001-acknowledgements.md",
      "source_hash": "947f1c4e2a7e5746fa552c586b6904e0d94653bb5edb1b1c21a43a44ca578f79",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Acknowledges the WHO programme staff, partner organizations and experts who contributed to the technical brief on advanced HIV disease in children and adolescents. It names contributors from bodies such as ICAP, the Elizabeth Glaser Pediatric AIDS Foundation, the Clinton Health Access Initiative and Médecins Sans Frontières.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "source": "sections/sec-002-background.md",
      "source_hash": "a3bba265202a4d30dba8859ce7e0cedd51aa44d1d97df83f7636ff290b4297ee",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out the main causes of illness and death in children with HIV in low- and middle-income countries, such as pneumonia, TB and malnutrition, and explains that the brief builds on WHO's 2017 advanced HIV disease guidelines. It notes that many interventions also apply to children without advanced disease.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "source": "sections/sec-003-current-who-guidelines-on-managing-advanced-hiv.md",
      "source_hash": "9779ab0e45232576f3e0189dca351656897d18cf7a794684f45cdb898e14ec10",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Summarizes WHO's 2017 guidance on advanced HIV disease, defining it for children and noting that all children under five are considered to have advanced disease, with exceptions for those stable on treatment. It explains that the evidence base comes mainly from adult trials such as REMSTART and REALITY. It then outlines the screening, prophylaxis and treatment recommendations relevant to children and adolescents, including that cryptococcal screening is not advised under age 10.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "source": "sections/sec-005-tuberculosis.md",
      "source_hash": "9b1adefad9eb8f9978c6a6879502df3dde834fe603cbdd521941ef6304c9912e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the high incidence of TB in children with HIV and the symptoms used to screen for it, noting the overlap with other HIV-related signs. It covers the limits of urine LF-LAM testing in children, the 2019 LAM recommendations and the advantages of rapid molecular tests such as Xpert MTB/RIF, while stressing the continuing role of clinical diagnosis.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-cryptococcal-disease.md",
      "source_hash": "c555c52cd0c916ce78f10f10b4cae422c890ee796492c757c8742d7fde8cbb00",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that cryptococcal disease is rare in young children with HIV, so antigen screening is recommended only for adolescents, and lists useful WHO resources on TB diagnostics and HIV guidelines.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-tuberculosis.md",
      "source_hash": "58ac08b31a6f507c5c9e92060ac58713c3d85704cdfccca5adc28caa75234bd2",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes child-friendly fixed-dose TB treatment formulations and how to manage drug interactions between rifampicin and lopinavir/ritonavir or dolutegravir in children with HIV.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-severe-pneumonia.md",
      "source_hash": "94efbaab6ae7aff1575cdaaeeb5bbde6345bc700fefcff93dbb896d9d20b49de",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Covers the bacterial causes of severe pneumonia in children with HIV, classification by IMCI algorithms and high-dose co-trimoxazole for suspected Pneumocystis pneumonia in young infants. It notes that for children aged one to five, standard WHO antibiotics are preferred over co-trimoxazole.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-332907/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-severe-bacterial-infections.md",
      "source_hash": "93c5c6fdf7abeb4611bcb20a53fb964d2e588e5f89383ab250c17297aaa8be2b",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes high rates of bacteraemia in children starting antiretroviral therapy and the pathogens involved, advising treatment according to WHO guidelines.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
